## Context

Child of master ticket 0650. This child owns the single slow/integration
instrument specified by the `R13, the soak gate` bullet in `SPEC.md` §5.2.8.
It consumes 0651's answer-survival assertion and 0652's commit/work accounting;
it must not grow substitute versions of either. Ticket 0035 owns obtaining the
real multi-process implementation, not this harness.

## Actions

- Implement the exact workload, topology, fault schedule, metrics and service
  cases named in `SPEC.md` §5.2.8, reading or citing its numbers rather than
  copying them into another authority.
- Capture raw latency, SQLite-error, WAL, lease-transition, commit, work-counter,
  fault and process-lifetime evidence sufficient to recompute every verdict.
- Prove each injected kill and freeze occurred. An unfired fault is `not-run`.
- Keep deterministic mechanism fixtures in the fast suite and expose the real
  machine/corpus run as an explicit slow gate. Missing substrate is never PASS.

## Test

- [ ] Each metric detector has a focused red control.
- [ ] Kill, freeze and cold-service controls prove their preconditions fired.
- [ ] A reduced mechanism fixture is labeled as such and cannot be emitted as
      the full soak verdict.
- [ ] The complete run consumes 0651 and 0652's checks without duplicating them.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] The complete §5.2.8 R13 soak runs against an eligible real target.
- [ ] Every specified metric and service clause receives an evidence-backed
      verdict in a committed `bench/results/` artifact.
- [ ] The slow-gate command, machine disclosure and reproduction procedure are
      documented next to the driver.
- [ ] Generated acceptance reporting includes the soak without confusing it
      with fixture coverage.
- [ ] `make check`, the soak gate and `./tickets/erg check tickets/` pass.
